10. Automatic Licensing of Downstream Recipients.

Each time you convey a covered work, the recipient automatically
receives a license from the original licensors, to run, modify and
propagate that work, subject to this License. You are not responsible
for enforcing compliance by third parties with this License.

An "entity transaction" is a transaction transferring control of an
organization, or substantially all assets of one, to another. If an
entity transaction occurs between Parties A and B, the licenses
granted by A to B include all licenses granted by A to any licensee
or remote work connected through A. The same is true for licenses
granted by B through A.

Any attempt to copy or propagate a covered work that is not an entity
transaction and does not result in a separate license grant from a
copyright holder to a specific recipient is void, and every recipient
of the work covered by this License obtains their license from the
original licensor. If you convey a covered work, you do not need to
obtain any license from the recipients of the work.

You may not impose any further restriction on the exercise of the
rights granted or affirmed by this License. For example, you may not
impose a license fee, royalty, or other charge for exercise of any
right granted under this License, and you may not initiate litigation
(including a claim for patent infringement) alleging that any patent
claim is infringed by making, using, selling, offering for sale, or
importing the Program or any portion of it.

11. Patents.

A "contributor" is a copyright holder who authorizes use under this
License of a program or work under whose copyright you have the right
to use it under this License. A "patent license" is an express
agreement or commitment, not denominated as a license or patent, not
to enforce a patent (such as an option to purchase a patent, a waiver
of a right to sue under a patent, or an agreement not to sue on a
patent). To "grant" a patent license to a participant means to make
such an agreement or commitment not to enforce a patent against the
participant.

If you convey a covered work, knowingly relying on a patent license,
and the Corresponding Source of the work is not available for anyone
to copy, free of charge under the terms of this License, through a
publicly available network server or other readily accessible means,
then you must either (1) cause the Corresponding Source to be so
available, or (2) arrange to deprive yourself of the benefit of the
patent license applicable to this work, or (3) arrange, in a manner
consistent with the purposes of this License, to deprive anyone
downstream of any benefit of the patent license under this License.

Nothing in this License shall be construed as excluding or limiting
the use of patent licenses available under the GNU General Public
License version 3 or any later version.

